<title>GERMANY: Porsche -Boxster orders above forecast.</title>
<headline>Porsche -Boxster orders above forecast.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German sports car maker Dr. Ing. h. c. f. Porsche AG said on Tuesday orders for its new Boxster two-seater cabriolet were much better than expected.</p>
<p>Series production of the Boxster started in August.  </p>
<p>&quot;The order situation is significantly better than we had expected,&quot; management board chairman Wendelin Wiedeking told a news conference.</p>
<p>Porsche said earlier it planned to increase overall sales of 911 cars and Boxsters to 30,000 vehicles in the 1996/1997 financial year to July 31, from 20,000 in 1995/1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
